{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the whistle [Bb]blows each morning,
and I [F]walk down in that cold dark [Bb]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I say a prayer for my dear savior
please let me [F]see the [Bb]sunshine one more time.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When oh [G]when will it be [Bb]over
when [E]will I lay these [F]burdens down
[Bb]and when I die dear Lord in heaven
please take my [D]soul from beneath that cold dark [G]ground.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I still greive for my poor brother
and I still hear my dear ol mother cry.
But late that night they came an told her
he lost his life down in the vanleer mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I have no shame I feel no sorrow
if on this earth not much I own
I have a love for my sweet children
an ol plow mule a shovel and a hoe.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Repeat last line of chorus and end.
{end_of_chorus}
